00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.440
Are you trying to be rich
because you wanna go buy shit

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.290
to create a perception that you're happy?

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.090
Or do you actually want to be happy?

00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:27.280
- Yeah!

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.630
- You got your perspective.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.523
I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.810
So listen, I think there's two core things

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.290
that I wanna think about,

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.240
which is, there's a lot of ways I say it,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.710
macro, micro, perspective and execution.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.540
When I think about why the 9,000 of you

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.540
would allocate time and
money to come to an event,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.540
it means that there is a need
for offense, more offense,

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.820
getting out of defense, offense.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.376
To me, this is about one big conversation.

00:01:09.376 --> 00:01:12.220
(laughing and cheering)

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.010
One big conversation of what
are we actually doing here?

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.150
And so, for me, when I think
about what are we actually

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.950
doing here, the first thing
that always comes to mind,

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.580
and I know some of you
have heard this from me,

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.440
but the fact that the odds
of being a human being

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.340
are 400 trillion to one is
something that I struggle with

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.850
not thinking about
almost on a daily basis.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.030
I genuinely believe that every person

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.400
in this arena right now, including myself,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.450
disproportionately aren't
understanding how fortunate

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.770
we are to have a life.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.660
There is literally nothing,
there's literally nothing

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.740
that you will ever accomplish, ever,

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.040
that is more ridiculous than
the fact that you were even

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.560
given a life in the first place.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.570
The fact that your mom could've got up

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:03.790
and got another glass of wine,
(laughing)

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.190
and that would result
in you not being here,

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.370
or a human, blows my mind.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:12.660
And so, for me, one of the
things that I clearly am

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.020
is optimistic and positive,

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.430
but I'm disproportionately practical.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.140
The great fortune of my
life was that I was born

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.980
in the Soviet Union and I came to America,

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.950
and my parents were poor and
we lived in a studio apartment

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.290
with multiple family members,
and I wasn't given anything,

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.780
and I genuinely believe the biggest issue

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.430
for so many people in today's
world to get to happiness,

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.890
forget about how you
define success from a money

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.240
or a business standpoint,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.590
is I just think most people are entitled.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.400
I think that most people are entitled

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.520
and genuinely believe that
they deserve something,

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.560
and I think when you come from zero

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.940
and you come from such a nasty
place, like Soviet Russia,

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.600
the framework that I was brought up in

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.100
was lack of entitlement,
nobody owes you shit,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.500
and if you wanna accomplish something,

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.930
you've gotta do something about it.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.120
And, for me...
(cheering)

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.260
Because let me promise
you something right now,

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.120
if you look to the left and right of you,

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.470
like, no matter what your
problems or short comings

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.500
or lack of opportunities are,

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.590
the person to the left and
right of you has their own life

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.350
and aren't worried about your dumb shit

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.300
'cause they've got their own dumb shit.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.560
And so, for me, my mom, basically,

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.950
'cause my dad worked every hour

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.810
so I didn't really even know
him until I started working

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.470
in the liquor store as a teenager,

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.120
my mom's lack of interest in any excuse

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.460
created a framework for me.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.450
So, for me, what's interesting about that

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.670
is that made me positive, not negative.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.830
What's amazing about being
in a place where you realize

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.970
nothing is entitled is
you get into a place

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.490
of full accountability.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.660
Genuinely, I believe that
every problem I have,

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.130
I run a 1,000 person, $200
million marketing company,

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.670
Vana Media, and literally,
every single problem

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.680
in that company, and let me promise you,

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.350
there's 40,000 fucking
problems right this second

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.060
as I'm on this stage,

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.640
every one of those problems are my fault

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.970
because instead of what I watch
so many people do and say,

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.220
oh, fucking Susan's fucking up,

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.694
I realize that I'm the
fuck-face that hired Susan.

00:04:20.694 --> 00:04:24.620
(laughing and applauding)

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.640
My friends, I'm coming out the gate here

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.580
